    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and all its tests pass along with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nThe implementation is complete. Summary of changes to `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Added a `normalizeAddress` helper** that trims, collapses internal whitespace to single spaces, upper-cases, and expands street-type abbreviations on a whole-word basis (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). A `null` or blank-after-trim value normalizes to an empty string. Abbreviations are held in an `ADDRESS_ABBREVIATIONS` map.\n\n2. **Normalization on create**: in `addOwner`, the owner's address is set to the normalized form before household processing, so the stored and returned `address` is normalized.\n\n3. **Required-field check**: the `address` check now tests `isBlank(normalizeAddress(...))`, so an address that is blank after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"`) is rejected with 400.\n\n4. **Household comparisons use the normalized form**: because `owner.setAddress(...)` is applied before `applyHousehold`, both duplicate detection and the shared `householdId` derivation operate on the normalized address (owners created through this endpoint store normalized addresses, keeping comparisons consistent).\n\n`updateOwner` was intentionally left unchanged, since the spec scopes normalization to owner creation.",
